WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.593 --> 00:00:18.624
"Oof!" Zann landed so hard that his head spun.

2
00:00:19.605 --> 00:00:21.727
He stayed still for a moment to catch his breath.

3
00:00:22.708 --> 00:00:24.589
Finally he was able to sit up.

4
00:00:25.450 --> 00:00:27.231
There was no sign of the sand beast.

5
00:00:28.112 --> 00:00:28.873
That was a relief.

6
00:00:29.633 --> 00:00:32.436
But there was no sign of Zann's friends or Wyssa either.

7
00:00:33.280 --> 00:00:35.962
"I guess that's why Wyssa didn't want us to zap," he muttered.

8
00:00:36.843 --> 00:00:40.945
Looking around, he realized he'd landed in some kind of deep gully.

9
00:00:41.566 --> 00:00:43.067
It looked like a dry riverbed.

10
00:00:43.087 --> 00:00:46.129
"That figures," Zann told himself.

11
00:00:47.089 --> 00:00:51.873
Whenever he zapped without focusing on his destination, he always seemed to land in water.

12
00:00:52.633 --> 00:00:57.056
He supposed that this gully was the closest thing there was to water in the dry expanse of

13
00:00:57.076 --> 00:00:58.017
the Far Frontier.

14
00:00:58.877 --> 00:01:00.518
Thinking about water made him thirsty.

15
00:01:01.259 --> 00:01:02.620
But he tried to ignore that feeling.

16
00:01:03.444 --> 00:01:06.387
He needed to find his friends before he did anything else.

17
00:01:07.487 --> 00:01:09.389
Zann climbed to his feet with a groan.

18
00:01:10.210 --> 00:01:13.192
The rocky gully hadn't been as soft a landing as the sand!

19
00:01:13.993 --> 00:01:15.454
He approached the gully's bank.

20
00:01:16.234 --> 00:01:20.898
When he tried to climb it, every rock he touched came loose and tumbled to the ground.

21
00:01:21.739 --> 00:01:24.621
He grabbed a gnarled shrub that was growing out of the bank.

22
00:01:25.162 --> 00:01:27.964
But the shrub's branches were lined with sharp thorns.

23
00:01:28.985 --> 00:01:33.008
Soon he was filthy, sore, and totally discouraged.

24
00:01:33.836 --> 00:01:35.197
"This is ridiculous."

25
00:01:35.838 --> 00:01:37.519
Zann pulled a thorn from his palm.

26
00:01:37.539 --> 00:01:42.063
"Maybe zapping didn't work exactly how I expected it to, but it still worked."

27
00:01:42.944 --> 00:01:45.526
That meant using magic wasn't out of the question.

28
00:01:46.306 --> 00:01:47.848
It didn't matter what Wyssa had said.

29
00:01:49.069 --> 00:01:50.190
Zann snapped his fingers.

30
00:01:50.210 --> 00:01:53.753
"Levitate." For a second nothing happened.

31
00:01:54.693 --> 00:01:57.376
Zann frowned, and then he rubbed his hands together.

32
00:01:58.156 --> 00:02:00.658
Magic energy began to spark weakly around him.

33
00:02:00.678 --> 00:02:03.701
"Levitate!" he said loudly.

34
00:02:04.562 --> 00:02:07.264
This time he felt his feet lift off the sand.

35
00:02:08.065 --> 00:02:11.828
He kept rubbing his hands, and slowly he rose into the air.

36
00:02:12.709 --> 00:02:14.791
Then he felt himself sinking again.

37
00:02:14.811 --> 00:02:19.435
"Levitate!" he cried again, rubbing his legs together too.

38
00:02:20.376 --> 00:02:23.779
Finally he managed to levitate all the way out of the gully.

39
00:02:24.579 --> 00:02:26.181
He landed on the sand at the edge.

40
00:02:26.201 --> 00:02:27.942
"Whew," he said.

41
00:02:27.962 --> 00:02:33.719
"Hey!" A swarm of insects buzzed around him, stinging his arms and face.

42
00:02:34.459 --> 00:02:36.701
Zann swatted at them, but they kept attacking.

43
00:02:37.401 --> 00:02:40.143
When he tried to zap them with magic energy, he missed.

44
00:02:40.163 --> 00:02:44.166
"Ouch!" he yelled, trying to smack one of the insects.

45
00:02:44.886 --> 00:02:45.847
But it was too fast.

46
00:02:46.828 --> 00:02:49.350
Zann rubbed his hands together, ready to zap away.

47
00:02:50.110 --> 00:02:50.851
He hesitated.

48
00:02:51.651 --> 00:02:54.053
What if he ended up even farther away from his friends?

49
00:02:55.094 --> 00:02:58.156
He danced in place, trying to avoid the stinging insects.

50
00:02:58.996 --> 00:03:02.137
His feet kicked up some sand, which gave him an idea.

51
00:03:02.977 --> 00:03:05.698
Zann dropped to his hands and knees and started to dig.

52
00:03:06.538 --> 00:03:11.339
He dug his way into the soft, warm sand until he was almost completely covered.

53
00:03:12.220 --> 00:03:13.820
Fewer insects could reach him now.

54
00:03:14.600 --> 00:03:18.481
The sand was hot, and after a few minutes, Zann couldn't stand it.

55
00:03:19.222 --> 00:03:23.023
He didn't hear any more buzzing, so he carefully dug his way back out.

56
00:03:23.763 --> 00:03:24.723
The insects were gone!

57
00:03:24.743 --> 00:03:31.125
"Thank goodness," he muttered, quickly healing the stings with magic.

58
00:03:31.965 --> 00:03:37.187
It took a few tries, since his magic energy kept fizzling out before he could touch the right

59
00:03:37.247 --> 00:03:41.048
spots. But finally his skin stopped burning and itching.

60
00:03:41.828 --> 00:03:43.909
But then Zann was thirstier than ever.

61
00:03:44.769 --> 00:03:48.790
Since his healing magic had basically worked, he snapped his fingers to create a drink.

62
00:03:49.910 --> 00:03:55.072
"Yuck!" he exclaimed as something soft and squishy appeared in his hand.

63
00:03:55.880 --> 00:04:02.265
Instead of a cup of refreshing airberry juice, he'd conjured a handful of squashed, overripe airberries!

64
00:04:02.285 --> 00:04:07.329
"Ugh!" Zann tossed the berries away and wiped his hand.

65
00:04:08.130 --> 00:04:09.111
Then he tried again.

66
00:04:10.071 --> 00:04:11.372
He focused carefully.

67
00:04:12.573 --> 00:04:13.454
This time it worked!

68
00:04:14.195 --> 00:04:17.377
He gulped the cup of airberry juice, which made him feel better.

69
00:04:18.558 --> 00:04:20.620
But why was magic so difficult here?

70
00:04:21.364 --> 00:04:26.027
At the Cave of the Unknown, it was partly because of all the powerful relics that had been

71
00:04:26.107 --> 00:04:26.667
hidden there.

72
00:04:27.347 --> 00:04:28.868
Could there be relics nearby now?

73
00:04:28.888 --> 00:04:32.890
"Maybe Morb stole the relics and hid them out here where nobody would find them!"

74
00:04:33.211 --> 00:04:34.391
Zann thought with a shiver.

75
00:04:35.272 --> 00:04:36.813
Just then he heard a sound.

76
00:04:37.573 --> 00:04:41.015
He spun around and saw Darb riding toward him on a hoof beast.

77
00:04:41.735 --> 00:04:43.716
Perda was sitting behind him, looking nervous.

78
00:04:44.337 --> 00:04:47.298
Two more hoof beasts were trotting along behind the first one.

79
00:04:47.318 --> 00:04:49.980
"I knew you could tame those animals!"

80
00:04:50.420 --> 00:04:52.802
Zann called, smiling, as his friends reached him.

81
00:04:53.943 --> 00:04:54.564
"Where's Gliss?"

82
00:04:54.584 --> 00:04:56.245
"We don't know."

83
00:04:57.206 --> 00:04:58.107
Perda jumped down.

84
00:04:58.127 --> 00:05:00.009
"We hoped she was with you."

85
00:05:00.029 --> 00:05:03.932
"We haven't seen Wyssa, either," Darb added.

86
00:05:04.813 --> 00:05:07.215
"Luckily Perda and I landed near each other."

87
00:05:08.316 --> 00:05:09.016
Perda nodded.

88
00:05:09.036 --> 00:05:11.679
"I ended up on a rocky little bluff.

89
00:05:12.279 --> 00:05:15.642
I looked around and spotted Darb on some grassland below me."

90
00:05:15.662 --> 00:05:20.233
"Grassland?" Zann looked around at the sand and rocks.

91
00:05:20.253 --> 00:05:24.555
"The grass was pretty brown," Darb said with a smile.

92
00:05:25.335 --> 00:05:26.756
He patted one of the hoof beasts.

93
00:05:27.576 --> 00:05:29.097
"But these guys were eating it."

94
00:05:29.117 --> 00:05:33.739
"Yeah, and as usual Darb made friends right away!"

95
00:05:34.119 --> 00:05:35.380
Perda said with a laugh.

96
00:05:35.400 --> 00:05:38.841
"So we decided to ride around and look for everyone.

97
00:05:38.861 --> 00:05:44.964
"You were only a ten-minute ride from where we landed," Darb said, scratching the hoof beast on the

98
00:05:45.024 --> 00:05:49.621
neck. "This guy must have smelled you or something, because he led us this way."

99
00:05:49.641 --> 00:05:51.842
"Good," Zann said.

100
00:05:51.862 --> 00:05:54.843
"Maybe that means he can help us find Gliss and Wyssa.

101
00:05:55.123 --> 00:05:56.443
They're probably nearby too."

102
00:05:57.703 --> 00:05:58.364
"I hope so."

103
00:05:58.924 --> 00:06:00.904
Darb whistled for the other two hoof beasts.

104
00:06:01.664 --> 00:06:04.865
"I'll show you how to ride these guys, and then we can start searching."

105
00:06:06.626 --> 00:06:11.847
Riding a hoof beast was like riding a dragon, except that the hoof beasts were furry instead of

106
00:06:11.927 --> 00:06:13.748
scaly, and they didn't fly.

107
00:06:14.588 --> 00:06:18.955
Zann held onto the creature's long, silky mane as he settled onto its back.

108
00:06:18.975 --> 00:06:21.459
"Come on," he told his hoof beast.

109
00:06:21.479 --> 00:06:23.241
"Let's find our friends."
